From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:20:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: TF_DS_ENGRAM_ROWCACHE_MB=N: a process-lifetime Engram row cache on every
 read path

The decode rounds read Engram rows through engram_aio's submit/wait and bypass prompt.readRows
entirely, and every read path hit the table files again: no bytes a rank had already read were ever
reused (prefix cache review finding 6).

TF_DS_ENGRAM_ROWCACHE_MB=N budgets N MiB of row payloads in a process-lifetime LRU keyed (layer
table id, row id), consulted and filled at every read path -- prompt.readRows (prompt chunks, the
read-ahead, the TF_DS_ENGRAM_LEAD readers and the pool fallback) and engram_aio's submit/wait,
hooked inside Aio.start/wait so the decode rounds and every other AIO reader are covered by one
seam (round.zig is untouched). With TF_DS_ENGRAM_SCALES=map only the weight bytes are cached; the
scales keep coming from the mapping. Otherwise both row parts (256 B FP8 + 8 B E8M0) are cached.
Read on each rank; the cache is byte-transparent and needs no cross-rank agreement (like
TF_DS_ENGRAM_LEAD), and start.sh's TF_DS_* passthrough carries it to both ranks unchanged.

Unset, 0, negative or non-numeric: no cache is allocated and every path is exactly the base code --
readRows falls through to pool.gather and each AIO batch submits all its reads; with the cache on,
hits copy to their output slots and misses read as before, landing in the cache at completion. A row
bigger than the whole budget is not cached at all, and a mapped-table entry serves weight-only
lookups and misses scale-requiring ones. The row cache's init is wired null-safe — `Model.open`
initializes field-by-field from undefined, so `Model.rc` is explicitly nulled at init (a crash found
and fixed before any pair run: with the cache off the undefined field poisoned every ring's consult).

Tests: zig build test and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh pass; the patch's own tests:
engram_io.zig's budget parse, the (table id, row id) keyed cache round-trip and the LRU byte-budget
cases, and prompt.zig's "a round's AIO read is served what a prompt read filled" integration test.
Not run on a pair.
---
